<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="38620" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EALC/495/38620.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="EALC" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EALC.xml">East Asian Language and Culture</subject><course id="495" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EALC/495.xml">Topics in Asian Religions</course></parents><sectionNumber>AT1</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Material Jainism</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 17-Mar-25 - 07-May-25.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Eight weeks, eight objects, one object a week. The course will guide you through the main aspects of Jainism by looking at its objects, including artworks (statues, manuscripts, etc.), but also items used in everyday life (the ascetic's clothes, teapots, etc.). The course offers a survey of Jainism through a selection of skillfully designed objects with the aim to convey the importance of material culture in understanding the Jain religious tradition.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-03-17Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2055</roomNumber><meetingDateRange>Meets 17-Mar-25 - 07-May-25.</meetingDateRange><buildingName>Sidney Lu Mech Engr Bldg</buildingName><instructors><inst